{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>A man lay with her.</b> This excludes a minor and one who is not a 'man' (Sifrei)." "<b>You lay with seed.</b> Her own lying disqualifies her; her sister's lying does not disqualify her (as in the case of two sisters who resembled each other)." "<b>And it was hidden from the eyes of her husband.</b> This excludes a blind man — but if he saw and shut his eyes, the waters do not test her (Sifrei)." "<b>And she was secluded.</b> The measure is that she be secludable for the defilement of intercourse." "<b>And there is no witness against her.</b> This means that if there is even one witness who said, 'You were defiled,' she would not drink (Sotah 4a)." "<b>And there is no witness against her.</b> For the defilement — but there are witnesses to the seclusion, as in (ibid. 2)." "<b>She is caught.</b> She is violated — as in ״וּתְפָשָׂהּ וְשָׁכַב עִמָּהּ״ (Deuteronomy 22)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {5 "Rashi's citation 'שם ב׳' ('there 2') refers back to a verse recently cited; the reference is to a passage concerning witnesses to seclusion."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:32.054088876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}